#sortorder:6
#showas:戴森动力学
Dyson Dynamics pits you against three AI opponents, as well as three Dyson Spheres.  It's a Tattered Honeycomb galaxy, and you'll command the Broadside fleet, which needs a deft hand at the controls but features a strong alpha strike capability.  

The AIs are reduced in difficulty to make tackling all of them a more palatable dask.  Sledge Hammer (difficulty 6) will test your defenses with the waves it sends, but has weaker warden and hunter fleets than you'd expect.  Bar Fighter (difficulty 5) will defend to it's best, while the Full Ensemble (difficulty 4) looks weak on paper, but has the warden and hunter of a difficulty 6 opponent.  These types of 'non-standard' AI balances can provide some interesting and unexpected twists.  

The Dyson Spheres are the Zenith which you are likely already familiar with, as well as the Gray and Chromatic Spire variants.  All of them can be irrelevant or fairly important depending on their placement in the galaxy, and all also provide the opportunity for exploitation if you are willing to pay the price.  